nodecode-cloudflare-sandbox is a rewrite of kiyo-e's kiyo-e/hermes-cloudflare-sandbox:

  https://github.com/kiyo-e/hermes-cloudflare-sandbox
  commit 75961d77109b185bdaeef650cc9f945df0aa0551
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 kiyo-e (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the client half of the plugin, in Common Lisp. Its protocol notes
(docs/protocol.md) are what client.lisp implements: the bearer token, the
workspace route, the NDJSON command stream with its mandatory exit event, the
error code in a failed HTTP body, the 409 that a changed configuration is,
the cancel/release/reset routes, and the rule that a request is never
replayed -- with the section's validation rules (an https origin, the
instance list, the image name, a hashed workspace identity) carried over from
config.py. Its shape is one agent-facing tool, cf_sandbox, and eval verbs,
instead of Hermes's terminal environment provider.

Left out, and why: the Worker itself (worker/ and container/hermes-exec.py) is
TypeScript and a container Dockerfile, and the cell does not bundle it -- it
stays the original repository's, deployed by the operator, which is also
where the billing and the token secret stay. Hermes's own shell wrapping (its
cwd markers, stdin plumbing, process handles and BaseEnvironment subclass) is
not rewritten: Nodecode's shell is its own, and the cell reaches the
container through the tool and the verbs above. The cancel route is
implemented only as the Worker's deadline -- the cell has no interactive
process handle to kill. Cloudflare Access service-token headers are not
carried; the section's token is the Worker's own bearer check.
